{
  "$comment": "One statement of what a stored browser session answers, for the three providers whose web session both Quota clients read. Each case replays `exchanges` as the queue of responses a provider gives, once for `validate` and once for `collect`: a request answers the exchange at its own position, and an operation that stops early leaves the rest of the queue unused. `expect.validated` is the proven session or the error category the validation fails with; `expect.snapshot` is the reading or `null`, and a `null` reading names its category in `snapshot_error`. Every failure names the provider's own `sources` entry, which is the rung both runtimes report.",
  "sources": {
    "codex": "chatgpt_web_usage_api",
    "claude": "claude_web_usage_api",
    "grok": "grok_web_billing_api"
  },
